{"authored" [{"question" "q-161653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,2\\le z\\le 3y+x}.\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/review.json" "file_sha256" "5224a73b7a087e4ea834d7b4687dc7569e3ea10bf4ff48a953a445b6a3d4fa5e" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "cd0c3b2221ce2df161f6a48c7599b6302cc7c37558a0709f58003a57126f23b8" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/verification.json" "basis" 2097 "rationale" "Remove only the isolated extraneous factor4. The real fibers are nonempty, inner length3y+x−2, y integral3x+33/2, x integral39. Preserve originalproblem/key39/all fields/answer identities and every other algebra line."} {"question" "q-161653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3y+x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[z]_{z=2}^{z=3y+x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3y+x-2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+xy-2y]}_{y=1}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(24+4x-8)-(\\frac{3}{2}+x-2)]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3x+\\frac{33}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}(2)-0 \\\\  & =39.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/review.json" "file_sha256" "5224a73b7a087e4ea834d7b4687dc7569e3ea10bf4ff48a953a445b6a3d4fa5e" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "cd0c3b2221ce2df161f6a48c7599b6302cc7c37558a0709f58003a57126f23b8" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/verification.json" "basis" 2097 "rationale" "Remove only the isolated extraneous factor4. The real fibers are nonempty, inner length3y+x−2, y integral3x+33/2, x integral39. Preserve originalproblem/key39/all fields/answer identities and every other algebra line."} {"question" "q-161653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "39"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/review.json" "file_sha256" "5224a73b7a087e4ea834d7b4687dc7569e3ea10bf4ff48a953a445b6a3d4fa5e" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "cd0c3b2221ce2df161f6a48c7599b6302cc7c37558a0709f58003a57126f23b8" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161653/verification.json" "basis" 2097 "rationale" "Remove only the isolated extraneous factor4. The real fibers are nonempty, inner length3y+x−2, y integral3x+33/2, x integral39. Preserve originalproblem/key39/all fields/answer identities and every other algebra line."} {"question" "q-161659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$\n\nInterpret the unchanged inequalities in real coordinates. The square root requires $2-x^2\\ge0$, so the actual nonempty $x$ projection is $[-\\sqrt2,\\sqrt2]$. Find the volume using this real domain." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/review.json" "file_sha256" "7bfe2048a42966fe3f403f9b1db9ed75b14581ad4d8396ab21ec1e702afd64c6" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a6f85a2e2c45f02ddc941a20561ed450b86da3d23c442ad6c7b535fd1bdff7cc" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/verification.json" "basis" 2095 "rationale" "Retain the original R inequalities, require their real domain, and distinguish actual volume8sqrt2/3 from the independently authorized signed polynomial recovery8/3. Add the missing mathematical answer with new field/answer identities; preserve source accepted8/3 and all historical fields."} {"question" "q-161659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The inequalities defining $R$ are retained exactly. In real coordinates, $\\sqrt{2-x^2}$ is defined only for $|x|\\le\\sqrt2$. These values also satisfy the printed nominal bound $-2\\le x\\le2$. Thus the actual real solid is equivalently\n\n$$R=\\{(x,y,z):-\\sqrt2\\le x\\le\\sqrt2,\\ 0\\le z\\le\\sqrt{2-x^2},\\ 0\\le y\\le2z\\}.$$\n\nIts volume is\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\nV&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2-x^2}}\\int_0^{2z}1\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\\\\\n&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\\int_0^{\\sqrt{2-x^2}}2z\\,dz\\,dx\\\\\n&=\\int_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}(2-x^2)\\,dx\n=\\left[2x-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-\\sqrt2}^{\\sqrt2}\n=\\frac{8\\sqrt2}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThe original source accepted $8/3$. That value is the ordinary signed polynomial integral $\\int_{-2}^{2}(2-x^2)\\,dx$. It does not give the volume of this real solid: the source square-root bounds are undefined for $\\sqrt2<|x|\\le2$. All five original choices are retained as alternatives, and $8\\sqrt2/3$ is added as the correct study answer." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/review.json" "file_sha256" "7bfe2048a42966fe3f403f9b1db9ed75b14581ad4d8396ab21ec1e702afd64c6" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a6f85a2e2c45f02ddc941a20561ed450b86da3d23c442ad6c7b535fd1bdff7cc" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/verification.json" "basis" 2095 "rationale" "Retain the original R inequalities, require their real domain, and distinguish actual volume8sqrt2/3 from the independently authorized signed polynomial recovery8/3. Add the missing mathematical answer with new field/answer identities; preserve source accepted8/3 and all historical fields."} {"question" "q-161659" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{3}"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/review.json" "file_sha256" "7bfe2048a42966fe3f403f9b1db9ed75b14581ad4d8396ab21ec1e702afd64c6" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "a6f85a2e2c45f02ddc941a20561ed450b86da3d23c442ad6c7b535fd1bdff7cc" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161659/verification.json" "basis" 2095 "rationale" "Retain the original R inequalities, require their real domain, and distinguish actual volume8sqrt2/3 from the independently authorized signed polynomial recovery8/3. Add the missing mathematical answer with new field/answer identities; preserve source accepted8/3 and all historical fields."} {"question" "q-161659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}},\\,0\\le y\\le 2z}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}{\\int }_{0}^{2z}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}2z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{z}^{2}]}_{z=-0}^{z=\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{(\\sqrt{2-{x}^{2}})}^{2}-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2-{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=-2}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2(2)-\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3})-(2(-2)-\\frac{1}{3}(-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =(4-\\frac{8}{3})-(-4+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161659" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2y,\\,0\\le x\\le y+2z}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}y+2z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{[yz+{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}y(2y)+(2y)^{2}-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}6{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[2{y}^{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =2(3)^{3}-2(1)^{3}-0 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161656" "fie