e_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{3y+x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}[z]_{z=2}^{z=3y+x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}3y+x-2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+xy-2y]}_{y=1}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(24+4x-8)-(\\frac{3}{2}+x-2)]\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}3x+\\frac{33}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{33}{2}(2)-0 \\\\  & =39.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacad