ce/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{33}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "39"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le z\\le 2+y,\\,1\\le x\\le y-z+3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}{\\int }_{1}^{y-z+3}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}[x]_{x=1}^{x=y-z+3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}(y-z+3)-1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2+y}y-z+2\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{[(y+2)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2+y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}((y+2)(2+y)-\\frac{(2+y)^{2}}{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{2}+4y+4\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+2{y}^{2}+4y]}_{y=-2}^{y=0} \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3}+2(-2)^{2}+4(-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivaria