170be50b88b67d3ab9de.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/33d937ccc1ae72f5add46a9358af4427147205a072ca2848a44d61288e705235.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+\\frac{x}{2}+z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/9e7c6fad45d9d85bad5ca16a2000e4d44a1739ab70797e41ae94945a4ffb02ef.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+\\frac{x}{2}+z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x/2+z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=1+x/2+z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(1+\\frac{x}{2}+z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}1+\\frac{x}{2}+z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(1+\\frac{x}{2})z+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((1+\\frac{x}{2})(2)+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4+x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[4x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8+2)-0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capt