apture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le z{e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{z{e}^{x}}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[y]_{y=0}^{y=z{e}^{x}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}z{e}^{x}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{x}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{e}^{x}]_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{0}-{e}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\frac{1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\frac{e-1}{2e}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094