erification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{21}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the plane $x=-1$ and the surface $x=3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2},$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=1,$ $z=0,$ $z=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le x\\le 3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=-1}^{x=3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}-(-1)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(3{y}^{2}+1)z+{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{y}^{2}+1)(1)+{1}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{y}^{2}+2\\,dy \\\\  & =[{y}^{3}+2y]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & ={1}^{3}+2(1)-0 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloid $x=-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=-1+2{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =-1+2{z}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}\\le x\\le -1+2{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse ${y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}^{-1+2{z}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+2{z}^{2})-(-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{(1-{y}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{(1-{y}^{2})/2}}\\,1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}+(1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =2-2{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-3{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-2{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}-2{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}$ and $z=-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2} & =-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}\\le z\\le -1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}}^{-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+5{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})-(-3+6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of\n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2}}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/2}}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/2}}\\,2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+(2-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-3{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-5{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4-2{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=4{x}^{2}$ and $y=1-2{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & =1-2{z}^{2} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1-2{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the elipse $4{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{4{x}^{2}}^{1-2{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-2{z}^{2})-(4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{(1-4{x}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{(1-4{x}^{2})/2}}\\,1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1-4{x}^{2}}{2}+(1-2{z}^{2}-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2-8{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/math