_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloid $x=3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=1-{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =1-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-{y}^{2})-(3{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}}/2}^{\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}}/2}\\,1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{1-4{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-4{y}^{2})+\\frac{1}{4}(1-4{y}^{2})+(1-4{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-6{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3+6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3-9{y}^{2}-8{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{9}{2}{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}-6{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=-2+3{x}^{2}$ and $y=-4{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{6}/3}^{\\sqrt{6}/3}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3{x}^{2} & =-4{z}^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+3{x}^{2}\\le y\\le -4{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $3{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+3{x}^{2}}^{-4{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-4{z}^{2})-(-2+3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{6}/3}^{\\sqrt{6}/3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}}/2}^{\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}}/2}\\,2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{2-3{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2-3{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{2-3{x}^{2}}{4}+(2-3{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =3-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "44954716125f0fe9cdf4719fc91e1d6cbf920b220a1bde53d11db47b973b90dc" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/state.json" "file_sha256" "217ab6b089dab9a6980216e821097024487dc65669dd1810309bd108144eba71" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161719" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-w