c7b0a56.png) runs from the surface\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/a0569d8f914ef9ad9e121ee79be25a1decce6381aedf54e3eb5ef633f652fe8e.png)\nup to the plane\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/0f1adb561fc36d233b9c2711b7da31566c8e9475b3ac442677963c5fdf54e5ac.png)\n\nSo we can write:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/f2c48bb89e04bcbf32e367ed0cdf260f7fa0630b3039f0fd842bfd418a5b124e.png)\n\nTherefore, the volume of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/f49bc07ef2d4d420878a9a9a3fab238aa47bed7fb96828ab0249cfd0c7419484.png) is given by the following triple integral:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/37f11eb812a19788af700184269ef20eb4cef4115fef59477afb49da067d940f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/example-8191.json" "file_sha256" "b07e4f91937414dd8e208ad8308f03d4bbab13fd9720ba143a4e6530399c4aaa" "basis" 2094 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-26133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/9145bfbf3c349359595396d06807191dc666c03558e5943e18d6a356d3b52e80.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064036/assets/98d18317cb2e69f489be66c8a4244e90327ed05aa0de5633fb6c461d81936a89.png) whose v